# docs/book/02-types.md:66 § "Numbers" -- the doc writes `int big = 9223372036854775807`
# (int max). Its counterpart, int MIN, is the smallest value the type holds and
# any beginner will write it the same way.
# Expected: -9223372036854775808
void main():
    int lo = -9223372036854775808
    print(f"{lo}")
